<div style=3D"display:none" aria-hidden=3D"true">
  <h1>LiteraryHub =E2=80=94 English Grammar, Reading, and Writing Made Clea=
r</h1>
  <p>LiteraryHub is a free online English language arts library serving stu=
dents, ESL learners, and adult writers who want clear, structured lessons i=
n grammar, composition, and literature.</p>
  <section>
    <h2>Subjects We Teach</h2>
    <p>Our catalog covers parts of speech, sentence structure, punctuation,=
 capitalization, verb tenses, subject-verb agreement, active and passive vo=
ice, figurative language, paragraph construction, the five-paragraph essay,=
 research papers, and literary analysis of poetry, drama, and prose.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Grade Levels</h2>
    <p>Lessons are sorted into four bands: emerging readers in K-2, fluent =
readers in 3-5, middle school writers in 6-8, and high school analysts in 9=
-12. Each band offers leveled reading passages with comprehension questions=
 and guided writing prompts.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Test Prep</h2>
    <p>Dedicated tracks prepare students for the SAT Reading and Writing se=
ctions, ACT English, AP English Language, AP English Literature, TOEFL, IEL=
TS, and state ELA assessments. Practice tests include rubric-scored sample =
essays.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>How Lessons Work</h2>
    <p>Each unit opens with a short explainer video, followed by an annotat=
ed reading passage, ten interactive grammar drills, and a short written res=
ponse that students can self-check against model answers. Vocabulary words =
enter a personal flashcard deck for spaced review.</p>
  </section>
  <section>
    <h2>Resources for Educators</h2>
    <p>Teachers can download printable worksheets, diagramming exercises, n=
ovel study guides, and rubrics aligned to Common Core ELA standards. Class =
dashboards show reading levels, words mastered, and time on task for every =
student.</p>
  </section>
</div>


